WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:16.935
Unit thirty-eight: Linking Words (because / so / although). Today you will join ideas with reason, result and contrast.

4
00:00:17.235 --> 00:00:19.934
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.272
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:26.129
Because.

7
00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:28.907
Because means used to give a reason.

8
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:31.563
I stayed home because I was ill.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.220
Your turn. Say: Because.

10
00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.126
Because.

11
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:40.606
So.

12
00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:43.326
So means used to give a result.

13
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:45.893
I was ill, so I stayed home.

14
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:48.694
Your turn. Say: So.

15
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:52.604
So.

16
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.270
Although.

17
00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:57.585
Although means used to show a contrast.

18
00:00:58.183 --> 00:01:00.136
Although it was cold, we went out.

19
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.147
Your turn. Say: Although.

20
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:06.978
Although.

21
00:01:07.717 --> 00:01:08.706
However.

22
00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:12.924
However means used to show a contrast between sentences.

23
00:01:13.517 --> 00:01:15.960
It was cold. However, we went out.

24
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.877
Your turn. Say: However.

25
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:22.595
However.

26
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.119
Reason.

27
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.163
Reason means the cause of something.

28
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.821
What is the reason?

29
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.814
Your turn. Say: Reason.

30
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:35.401
Reason.

31
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.012
Result.

32
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:40.655
Result means what happens because of something.

33
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.588
The result was good.

34
00:01:43.183 --> 00:01:45.325
Your turn. Say: Result.

35
00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:49.203
Result.

36
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:50.951
Contrast.

37
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.296
Contrast means a clear difference between two ideas.

38
00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:57.326
There is a contrast.

39
00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.732
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

40
00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:04.695
Contrast.

41
00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:06.138
But.

42
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.672
But means used to show a different idea.

43
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:11.818
It is small but strong.

44
00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.535
Your turn. Say: But.

45
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.006
But.

46
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.335
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.183 --> 00:02:26.347
Visal, why did you stay at home? Use because.

48
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:38.908
I stayed at home because I was ill. Because gives a reason. So gives a result: I was ill, so I stayed at home. The same idea can be said in two ways.

49
00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:41.029
And although?

50
00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:56.489
Although shows a contrast: Although it was cold, we went out. It means the cold did not stop us. However also shows contrast, but it joins two sentences: It was cold. However, we went out.

51
00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:58.782
Any rules?

52
00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:14.279
Do not use although and but together. Use a comma after a leading although-clause. Use a full stop or semicolon before however. Because needs a clause: because I was ill, not because of ill.

53
00:03:15.433 --> 00:03:16.760
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:17.617 --> 00:03:21.845
Grammar focus: Linking words: because and so and although and however.

55
00:03:22.145 --> 00:03:23.402
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:26.058
I stayed at home because I was ill.

57
00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.077
I was ill, so I stayed at home.

58
00:03:29.983 --> 00:03:31.913
Although it was cold, we went out.

59
00:03:32.867 --> 00:03:39.513
Because = reason, so = result, although / however = contrast. Do not use although and but together.

60
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.669
Be careful! Don't say: Although it rained, but we went.

61
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:47.644
Say: Although it rained, we went.

62
00:03:47.944 --> 00:03:49.886
Do not use although and but together.

63
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.155
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.281
Because, So, Although.

65
00:03:55.581 --> 00:03:57.778
I stayed at home because I was ill.

66
00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:01.126
I was ill, so I did not go to school.

67
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.702
Although it was cold, we went out to play.

68
00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:08.225
It was cold. However, we had fun.

69
00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.686
These linking words make our ideas clear.

70
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.906
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.842
I took an umbrella blank it was raining.

72
00:04:20.142 --> 00:04:23.355
A, because. B, so. C, although.

73
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.283
The answer is A: because.

74
00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:32.683
It was raining, blank I took an umbrella.

75
00:04:32.983 --> 00:04:36.567
A, because. B, so. C, although.

76
00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:41.843
The answer is B: so.

77
00:04:42.983 --> 00:04:44.902
blank it was late, we kept working.

78
00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:48.460
A, Because. B, So. C, Although.

79
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.058
The answer is C: Although.

80
00:04:55.217 --> 00:04:56.903
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.203 --> 00:05:03.445
A, Although it rained, but we went.. B, Although it rained, we went.. C, Although it rained so we went..

82
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.859
The answer is B: Although it rained, we went..

83
00:05:11.017 --> 00:05:14.282
According to the reading, why did the writer stay at home?

84
00:05:14.582 --> 00:05:19.431
A, because of illness. B, because of rain. C, because of work.

85
00:05:22.967 --> 00:05:25.326
The answer is A: because of illness.

86
00:05:26.533 --> 00:05:29.720
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:30.583 --> 00:05:33.279
Write one sentence with 'because' and one with 'although'.

88
00:05:42.083 --> 00:05:43.618
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:43.918 --> 00:05:53.470
I like English because it opens many doors. Although it is difficult, I practise every day. I use because for a reason and although for a contrast.

90
00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:55.398
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.283 --> 00:06:02.105
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and linking words: because and so and although and however.

92
00:06:02.405 --> 00:06:07.263
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

93
00:06:07.563 --> 00:06:10.100
See you in Unit thirty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.704
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

